{"title":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","category":"Engineering","bank":"nta_abhyas_jee_main","subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","count":9,"questions":[{"id":93328,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"A mixture of two gasses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is kept in a vessel which is maintained at a temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. In the vessel there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math> molecules each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>, of the gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></math> molecules each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math> of the gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. The mean square velocity of the molecules of the gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and the mean square velocity of the molecules of the gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> along the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> direction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math> is","options":["<math> <mtext>2</mtext></math>","<math> <mtext>1</mtext></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"Mean kinetic energy of the two types of molecules should be equal. The mean square velocity of A type molecules  <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> <br/><br/>Therefore,  <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> <br/><br/>This gives  <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e8637d01bf5ec7fe198b"},{"id":93329,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"Two identical vessels contain two different ideal gases at the same temperature. If the average speed of gas molecules in the first vessel is equal to the most probable speed of molecules in the second vessel, then the ratio of the mass of gas molecules in the first vessel to that in the second vessel is","options":["<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi>avg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><msub><mi>πM</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi>mp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mfrac></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e863a7a393bbbd066da2"},{"id":93330,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"Two vessels separately contain two ideal gases <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math> and <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math> at the same temperature, the pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> being twice that of <math> <mtext>B</mtext></math>. Under such conditions, the density of <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math> is found to be <math> <mtext>1.5</mtext> </math> times the density of <math> <mtext>B</mtext></math>. The ratio of molecular weights of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>A</mtext></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>B</mtext></math> is","options":["<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mn>2</mn></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mi>RT</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mi>RT</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ρ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e8630d2f33abe380f325"},{"id":93331,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"Under standard conditions, the density of a gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.3</mn><mtext> </mtext><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">mg cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> and the velocity of propagation of sound, in it, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>330</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The number of degrees of freedom of gas is","options":[],"answer":"5","solution":"<p><math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math> and <math><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>×</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mi>P</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>330</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>×</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>40</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e86360035d73b0158c2d","correctValue":"5","questionType":"numerical","type":"numerical"},{"id":93332,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"If the average kinetic energy of a molecule of hydrogen gas at <math><mn>300</mn><mi> </mi><mn>K</mn></math> is <math><mi>E</mi></math>, then the average kinetic energy of a molecule of nitrogen gas at the same temperature is","options":["<math><mn>7</mn><mi>E</mi></math>","<math><mn>14</mn><mi>E</mi></math>","<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>","<math><mi>E</mi></math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"We know that,<br/><br/>Kinetic energy <math><mo>∝</mo><mi>T</mi></math> <br/><br/>In the question, temperature is same in both conditions. So, the kinetic energy in the second condition is <math><mi>E</mi></math> .","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e8634525536ed136e630"},{"id":93333,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"An iron rocket fragment initially at<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> enters the earth's atmosphere almost horizontally and quickly fuses completely in atmospheric friction. Specific heat of iron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>11</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kcal</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mo>°</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, its melting point is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1535</mn><mo> </mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and the latent heat of fusion is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kcal</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>kg</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The minimum velocity with which the fragment must have entered the atmosphere is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><mi>km</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>32</mn><mo> </mo><mi>km</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><div id=\"gtx-trans\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 76px; top: -5.77778px;\"><div class=\"gtx-trans-icon\"> </div></div>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>32</mn><mo> </mo><mi>km</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><div id=\"gtx-trans\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 76px; top: -5.77778px;\"><div class=\"gtx-trans-icon\"> </div></div>","Zero"],"answer":1,"solution":"The kinetic energy of the fragment is changed to heat. Expressing mass m in kilograms everywher, we have<br /><br /> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mtext>0.11</mtext></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn><msup><mn>5</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn><mn>4</mn></math><br /><br /> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>≃</mo><mtext>1.76</mtext><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math><br /><br />Hence<br /><br /> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><msqrt><mtext>1.76</mtext></msqrt></mfenced><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mtext>1.32 km s</mtext><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e8637649047d29cfcbd2"},{"id":93334,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"The temperature of an ideal gas is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> . If the <math><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>s</mi></math> speed of the gas molecule is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> , then at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> it becomes","options":["<math><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></math>","<math><mn>4</mn><mi>V</mi></math>","<math><mn>0.5</mn><mi>V</mi></math>","<math><mi>V</mi></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<math><mo>∵</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> speed of molecule <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></math><br /><br />for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math><br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mn>100</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br />For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math><br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mn>400</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br />therefore, <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>100</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>400</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />or <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />or <math><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e863ef9a8058e376b098"},{"id":93335,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"In an ideal gas at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>, the average force that a molecule applies on the walls of a closed container depends on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> as <math><msup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></math>. A good estimate for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is","options":[],"answer":"1","solution":"The pressure exerted by molecules of a gas on the walls <math><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mi>p</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />But <math><mi>C</mi><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∝</mo><mi>T</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi>P</mi><mo>∝</mo><mi>T</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∵</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi></math> Force <math><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>A</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi>F</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e8630fdcd2605d519165","correctValue":"1","questionType":"numerical","type":"numerical"},{"id":93336,"subject":"Physics","chapter":"Kinetic Theory of Gases","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"The temperature at which a  molecule of nitrogen will have the same rms velocity as a  molecule of oxygen at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>127</mn><mo> </mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is ","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>457</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>273</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>77</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">℃</mi></math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"Root mean square velocity<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br />where <math><mi>R</mi></math> is gas constant, <math><mi>T</mi></math> the temperature and <math><mi>M</mi></math> molecular weight.<br /><br />Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msu